Apple appears to be sold out of the base <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/mac-mini/">Mac mini</a>, and the machine is listed as “Currently Unavailable” from the Apple Online Store. <br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2025/11/mac-mini-cyber.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1028593" /><br/>
The base &zwnj;Mac mini&zwnj; is the model with an M4 chip, 256GB of storage, and 16GB RAM. <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/m4-mac-mini/">M4 Mac mini</a> models with upgraded storage are still in stock, as are &zwnj;Mac mini&zwnj; models that are equipped with the M4 Pro chip. Configurations with 24GB RAM are also still available, but some models that use 32GB RAM or higher are out of stock.<br/>
<br/>
When an Apple device goes out of stock, it can be an indication of an imminent refresh, but it’s not clear if that’s the case with the &zwnj;Mac mini&zwnj;. The &zwnj;Mac mini&zwnj; has been in high demand because people are purchasing it to use as a machine to run AI models locally, so it’s possible the shortage is related to demand rather than a sign that an update is coming soon.<br/>
<br/>
Apple is also dealing with RAM shortages caused by a surge in global memory demand that has led to increased RAM pricing. The memory shortages previously caused some higher tier &zwnj;Mac mini&zwnj; and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/mac-studio/">Mac Studio</a> models to go out of stock. Apple removed the 512GB &zwnj;Mac Studio&zwnj; from its online store entirely earlier this year. <br/>
<br/>
Apple is working on M5 and M5 Pro versions of the &zwnj;Mac mini&zwnj; for 2026, but the update may not come until later in the year due to the RAM supply issues.<br/>
